{"type":"message","id":"94095cf4","parentId":"f39ffca6","timestamp":"2026-10-06T05:56:49.932Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Acknowledged. My task is read-only analysis anyway — no hardware writes. Continue.\n\nNow I have INF. Note: `AddService = ,%SPSVCINST_ASSOCSERVICE%` and service is user-mode exe. No .sys. Class System, HWID ACPI\\LHK2019.\n\nNow let me finalize the remaining research:\n1. Check fnhotkey dump for camera state reading — my grep found nothing for \"switch_camera\" etc. in the wide dump? It returned \"No matches found\" for strings-fnhotkeyutility.exe.txt — but that file is the wide dump and should contain those. Wait, earlier grep on strings16-fnhotkey found them. The wide dump (ASCII strings, `strings-...`) may not contain UTF-16 strings; those camera strings are UTF-16, hence only in strings16. And \"switch_camera\" (ASCII, lowercase) — hmm, \"_Thread_switch_camera\" appeared in strings16 as `MsgLogic g_HandleEvent e_Event_HID_SUPERKEY CreateThread _Thread_switch_camera Line: %d` — that's UTF-16. So in ASCII dump absent. OK.\n\nLet me grep strings16-fnhotkey for \"switch_camera\" and \"Camera\" pairs, and the switch/OSD flow. Already have lines 892,901-906,946,966,974,977,1000-1001. \n\nAlso check \"UtilityLSK2.0Status\" and event data. Let me grep strings16-fnhotkey for \"LSK2\", \"wParam\", \"fn_keys\", \"FnQ\".\n\nActually I have enough. Let me also confirm what ludp.dll is: it's the Lenovo User Data Platform / telemetry (\"hudson/workspace/Ludp.Win.sdk\", SQLite event DB, INSERT INTO ludp_event). So it's telemetry/analytics, unrelated to camera.\n\nLet me quickly identify mmstate.dll = mic-mute state (lsm). And controllib.dll = hardware control (ControlAPI). intelcontrollib = Intel Adapter ControlAPI. Already evidenced.\n\nLet me check controllib.dll strings for what it does (camera control?). The grep for \"Camera\" in controllib.dll returned no matches, so controllib has no camera API. Good.\n\nBut wait, fnhotkey's \"CameraPrivacy SwitchCameraStatus\" uses CoCreateInstance/BindToObject/pMoniker — that's likely `ICameraControl`? Let me grep the wide dump for \"Moniker\"/\"nIndexCamera\"/\"pCameraControl\". Those are in strings16 too. Let me read a chunk around lines 405-420 in the wide dump (ASCII) — no. Read strings16 lines 400-420. Let me do that.\n\nAlso grep for \"Camera\" alone in strings16-fnhotkey to gather all camera lines.\n\nLet me also grep all evidence for \"SW_CAMERA\"? no.\n\nLet me run final greps and then compose.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_OXcWfGsBnJIM5oeXUyZ46197","name":"grep","arguments":{"i":"Grep all camera lines in fnhotkey utf16","pattern":"amera|camera|Blur|blur|LVF|SmartAppearance|LSK2","path":"/home/user/Downloads/lenovo-camera-switch-re/70-evidence/strings16-fnhotkeyutility.exe.txt","case":true,"gitignore":false,"skip":null},"partialArgs":"{\"i\": \"Grep all camera lines in fnhotkey utf16\", \"pattern\": \"amera|camera|Blur|blur|LVF|SmartAppearance|LSK2\", \"path\": \"/home/user/Downloads/lenovo-camera-switch-re/70-evidence/strings16-fnhotkeyutility.exe.txt\", \"case\": true, \"gitignore\": false, \"skip\": null}","streamIndex":0,"intent":"Grep all camera lines in fnhotkey utf16"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_oFmXzZ26zoendNKHcvF91559","name":"grep","arguments":{"i":"Grep controllib purpose strings","pattern":"ControlAPI|Adapter|Gpio|LED|Battery|ReportID|HID","path":"/home/user/Downloads/lenovo-camera-switch-re/70-evidence/strings16-controllib.dll.txt","case":false,"gitignore":false,"skip":null},"partialArgs":"{\"i\": \"Grep controllib purpose strings\", \"pattern\": \"ControlAPI|Adapter|Gpio|LED|Battery|ReportID|HID\", \"path\": \"/home/user/Downloads/lenovo-camera-switch-re/70-evidence/strings16-controllib.dll.txt\", \"case\": false, \"gitignore\": false, \"skip\": null}","streamIndex":1,"intent":"Grep controllib purpose strings"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_iY9OEHdHIR3Vyu61